    "tree_id": "88e59e3c0e3832fee77a6c9f2d94797e59414214",
    "message": "ci: run the replay payload-bound tests in the capacity suite (#250)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe race shard `Go 1.27.1 race runtime-2` of the promotion pull request #249 exceeded the 30-minute `go test` timeout on two attempts (jobs 113180542606 and 113387018929). The shard took 31 minutes against 21 to 24 minutes before #247.\n\nThe compaction test from #247, `TestAcquisitionReplayCompactsSupersededMetadataBeforeRetainedBound`, crosses the 64 MiB retained payload bound with 6 MiB snapshots. It takes 610 seconds under race instrumentation and 25 seconds without it. Its sibling `TestAcquisitionReplayRejectsRetainedHistoryAboveBound` takes 215 seconds under race.\n\n## Change\n\n- `scripts/verification_tests.py` names every capacity test per package in `CAPACITY_TESTS`. The race suite passes `-skip` with the exact names and removes them from the shard expectation through `exclude_capacity`. The capacity suite runs only those names with `-run` and refuses a result that misses one.\n- `scripts/test_verification_tests.py` covers the exact pattern, the shard exclusion, and the capacity completeness check.\n- `docs/TESTING.md` records the capacity list.\n\nThe native non-race jobs still run every test, so the two replay tests keep their coverage there. The `Full Catalog Capacity` job step and `scripts/verify.sh` are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `python3 scripts/test_verification_tests.py`: 10 tests OK.\n- `go test ./internal/ciworkflow`: ok.\n- `python3 scripts/verification_tests.py capacity`: 6 of 6 pass in 619 seconds. The compaction test took 27 seconds and its sibling 8 seconds.\n- Shard listing check: shard runtime-2 lists 180 tests and expects 179 under race. The one exclusion is the compaction test.\n- `make technical-writing-check`: PASS.",
    "timestamp": "2026-10-08T16:42:09Z",
